{"name":"Maidenhair Fern","hex":"#44764a","fetched":"2026-10-12","looked":{"definitions":[{"term":"maidenhair fern","whole":true,"parts":[{"part":"Noun","definitions":["Maidenhair (Adiantum spp.)."]}],"link":"https://en.wiktionary.org/wiki/maidenhair_fern"}],"entries":[{"title":"Adiantum","blocks":[{"text":"Adiantum, the maidenhair fern, is a genus of about 250 species of ferns in the subfamily Vittarioideae of the family Pteridaceae, though some researchers place it in its own family, Adiantaceae. The genus name comes from Greek, meaning \"unwetted\", referring to the fronds' ability to shed water without becoming wet."}],"image":"https://thumb.wikimedia.org/wikipedia/commons/thumb/1/12/Adiantum_pedatum_09905.JPG/330px-Adiantum_pedatum_09905.JPG?utm_source=en.wikipedia.org&utm_campaign=api&utm_content=thumbnail","link":"https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Adiantum","wikidata":"Q673823"},{"title":"Fern","blocks":[{"text":"Ferns are a group of vascular plants that reproduce via spores and have neither seeds nor flowers. They reproduce in two phases, a short-lived gametophyte that reproduces sexually to develop a spore-bearing leaf structure. Some ferns produce coiled fiddleheads, which expand into fronds."}],"image":"https://thumb.wikimedia.org/wikipedia/commons/thumb/4/47/The_ferns_of_Great_Britain%2C_and_their_allies_the_club-mosses%2C_pepperworts%2C_and_horsetails_%28Pl._2%29_%288515393495%29.jpg/330px-The_ferns_of_Great_Britain%2C_and_their_allies_the_club-mosses%2C_pepperworts%2C_and_horsetails_%28Pl._2%29_%288515393495%29.jpg?utm_source=en.wikipedia.org&utm_campaign=api&utm_content=thumbnail","link":"https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Fern","wikidata":"Q80005"}],"images":[{"srcset":"https://thumb.wikimedia.org/wikipedia/commons/thumb/7/74/Adiantumhispidulum1web.jpg/120px-Adiantumhispidulum1web.jpg?utm_source=en.wikipedia.org&utm_campaign=parser&utm_content=thumbnail 1x, https://thumb.wikimedia.org/wikipedia/commons/thumb/7/74/Adiantumhispidulum1web.jpg/250px-Adiantumhispi